  "caption": "Initial March stratification and March mixed-layer depth in the Labrador-Irminger Seas (a,c) and Nordic Seas (b,d), with nine individual models shown in matching colors and no model-group mean curves. The piecewise-linear horizontal axes in a,b give equal visual spacing to0,1,2,4,6,8 without modifying the plotted physical N2 values. Black lines and gray bands show IAP March2005-2024 mean and interannual standard deviation using only observations within10-1000m; actual retained mid-depth levels are15-995m, without boundary extrapolation. The MLD curves retain the saved rectangular-region11yr centred means and missing end windows. The vertical dotted lines mark CO2 forcing reversal. Panels e-g show residual March MLD (final minus initial decades) for three fixed groups of3models: non-recovery (CESM2,CNRM-ESM2-1,UKESM1-0-LL), recovery (NorESM2-LM,GFDL-ESM4,CAS-ESM2-0), and larger bias (ACCESS-ESM1-5,CanESM5,MIROC-ES2L). Black contours show initial group-mean MLD at 200,400,600,800 and1000m. The filled scale spans-1000 to1000m, with extensions for values beyond that range and labelled ticks every500m. Initial and final ice edges are15percent contours of equal-weight group-mean annual SIC fields; the observed edge is the same NOAA/NSIDC1988-2020 annual climatology in all maps. All fixed members must have valid data for each averaged cell. No new smoothing, piControl correction or raw hydrographic computation is introduced.",
